  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who All-Star Music is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families of five or six who want a Value rate.</strong> The family suites sleep up to six, with a second bathroom and a kitchenette. In 2026 a Family Suite ran about $375 to $731 a night at full price, tax included.</li>
      <li><strong>Smaller parties watching the nightly rate.</strong> A Standard Room ran about $152 to $311 in 2026, in the same range as the other All-Stars.</li>
      <li><strong>Anyone who wants the largest Value-resort pool.</strong> Official pages list the guitar-shaped Calypso Pool at 251,418 gallons.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You want a sit-down restaurant at the hotel.</strong> There's a food court and a pool bar, and that's it.</li>
      <li><strong>You want Extended Evening Hours.</strong> Value resort guests don't get them.</li>
      <li><strong>You don't want to walk, and you booked a standard room.</strong> Preferred rooms sit closer to Melody Hall. Family suites are their own product; confirm the building when you book if the walk matters.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
