  <section id="booking">
    <h2>Booking and value tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Book a Standard Room if four people is enough and you don't mind walking.</strong> In 2026 those rooms ran about $152 to $311 a night at full price including tax, depending on dates. Preferred rooms ran about $199 to $364.</li>
      <li><strong>Book a Family Suite only if you will use the extra beds and the second bathroom.</strong> In 2026 those suites ran about $375 to $731. Compare that with two standard rooms, or with a family suite at Art of Animation, before you decide.</li>
      <li><strong>Extra adults cost more in the standard rooms.</strong> Value rates assume two adults. Each extra adult adds $15 a night plus tax, and kids under 18 are free. Tax at the All-Star resorts is 13.5%.</li>
      <li><strong>Check Disney's own offers page first.</strong> Disney points to <a href="https://disneyworld.disney.go.com/special-offers/">its special offers page</a> for discounts. Our deals hub will track current ones.</li>
      <li><strong>Lightning Lane head start:</strong> Disney resort guests can buy Lightning Lane passes up to 7 days before their stay.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="fg-callout">
      <h3>Rates change</h3>
      <p style="margin:0">The rate range above is MouseSavers' October 2026 snapshot of Disney's full prices, not a deal. Always check the live price on Disney's site before you book. Prices at this resort include 13.5% tax, which is higher than the 12.5% charged at most other Disney-owned Walt Disney World hotels.</p>
